Z||000000||Haze_Performance||04-02-2000||04:54 AM||||I have a 85 2M4 with the stock single (drivers side) exhaust pipe. I would like to install the V6 dual pipes (and muffler). My shop said no problem the V6 setup will bolt right up to the 4 banger. I dont see why it wont but before I spend the $375.00 I feel the need to ask around.     <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">  <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 04-02-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||04-02-2000||05:30 PM||||As long as the rear trim has the clearance for the duals then yes, the thing is a bolt in. The "dual" exhaust is only an extra outlet on the muffler and I think a diferant pipe from the cat to the muffler. Not sure about the pipe.||||reg||1
Z||000002||phillip||04-03-2000||07:56 AM||||  i just had this done a month ago on my '87 2.5. cut the plastic myself and had my own tips (big import boy style). gt muffler and installation $150. got a small discount. high flow cat $140.||||reg||1
